     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div>The data from Aeut comes from Grunwald and Hoheisel 2003: <a href=\"https://apsjournals.apsnet.org/doi/pdf/10.1094/PHYTO-96-1134\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://apsjournals.apsnet.org/doi/pdf/10.1094/PHYTO-96-1134&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792480362618000&amp;usg=AOvVaw04jXvppjO-qQDvzvq7NVua\">https://apsjournals.apsnet.org/doi/pdf/10.1094/PHYTO-96-1134</a>, but I think the data were obtained from a single primer set. <br><br></div>I believe it should be suitable to concatenate multiple tables as you describe, but I do not have sufficient knowledge of RAPD genotyping to confirm this. Does anyone else in the group have experience with RAPD genotyping and can share their expertise?<br><br></div><div>Best,</div><div>Zhian<br></div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div>"
    ],
