   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Thank you for the clarification! <br></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_attr\">Il giorno mar 29 ott 2019 alle ore 15:49 Niklaus Grünwald &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">niklaus....@gmail.com</a>&gt; ha scritto:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div>Hi Silvia,<div><br></div><div>Typically, each band on a RAPD gel is a dominant locus just as in AFLP scored as o and 1 for absence and presence. Homozygous (with two copies) is close to impossible to score.  Loci found for each primer combination can be concatenated into one large genotype sheet.</div><div><br></div><div>Best,</div><div>Nik<br><div><br><blockquote type=\"cite\"></blockquote></div></div></div></blockquote></div>"
    ],
